  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong multimodal baseline using the most capable components to set a high performance bar. Config_007 combines multimodal fusion (image + RNA), multiprofile (richer cellular information), scgpt (a pretrained single-cell foundation model, likely the strongest RNA encoder), imagenet_vit_l (a large pretrained vision encoder), avgpool (a simple, low-risk aggregation that avoids overfitting), and weighted fusion (flexible combination of modalities). This tests whether the strongest available encoder combination in a multimodal setting yields competitive accuracy. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can explore transformer aggregation, concat fusion, or singleprofile as logical extensions. If it underperforms, it signals that complexity or a specific encoder choice is the bottleneck, guiding targeted simplification. This is the best use of experiment 1 because it maximally reduces uncertainty about the overall multimodal pipeline quality while using the most informative (highest-capacity) configuration."
}

